 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Projective embedding over $X$",
 "statement": "Let $\\iota_Y:X'\\hookrightarrow\\mathbf P^n_Y$ be the closed immersion and\n$\\pi:X'\\to X$ the Chow modification. Then\n\n$$\n\\iota_X=(\\pi,\\iota_Y):X'\\longrightarrow\nX\\times_Y\\mathbf P^n_Y=\\mathbf P^n_X\n$$\n\nis a closed immersion over $X$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-proper-base-change/sk-thm-reduction/lemma-weil-pbc-chow-embedding-over-x.md",
  "place": "node lemma-weil-pbc-chow-embedding-over-x, order 1198"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-nagata-affine-proj",
  "def-nagata-projective-space-base-change"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The identification $\\mathbf P^n_X=X\\times_Y\\mathbf P^n_Y$ is the defining fibre-product\nidentity ([lemma-nagata-projective-space-base-change-pullback]), so the pair $\\iota_X=(\\pi,\\iota_Y)$ is a morphism over $X$ by construction, and\ncomposing it with the base change $\\mathbf P^n_X\\to\\mathbf P^n_Y$ of $f$ gives back\n$\\iota_Y$. That base change is separated, because $f$ is separated and separatedness is\nstable under base change. A morphism whose composite with a separated morphism is a closed\nimmersion is itself a closed immersion; hence $\\iota_X$ is a closed immersion.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-projective-space-base-change-pullback"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
